ong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.21), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1882. Lewiston's average high shows no clear change: +0.00\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.08 to +0.08) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.35\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.66) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.48\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.87). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 6 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; April and November fell.","t_rain":"Lewiston has gotten drier","p_rain":"Lewiston's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.18 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.30 to \u22120.06), about \u22122.6 inches since 1882. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 12.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1884 (21.76 in); the driest, 2007 (7.73 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 0 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}